    "scope": "14.d.W implements an owned artifact-import-plan-v1 observation from explicit parsed artifact candidates. Actual mapping bytes, native-owner lookup and the five-case policy derive regular create/update operations with explicit IDs, actor and time. The ordinary Change Plan service recomputes regular revisions/history and validates the complete supplied target. Exact input bytes, canonical and byte mapping hashes, candidate content, base/root, resource/source bindings and Change Plan hash are retained. Reports include planned created/updated IDs, skipped objects, unresolved conflicts, individual unaccepted unmapped-field losses and byte-verified existing attachment references. No-op/local/skip/reject preserve native history; safe adoption keeps the same ID and preserves unrelated fields and identities. A missing gate, divergent conflict, unaccepted loss or invalid complete target never exposes a valid executable plan. The regular saved plan reproduces the target on the same supplied model. No input parsing, filesystem completeness, authorization, transaction or completed import is claimed."
